# Logging Standards

## OBJETIVO

Estandariza logging para debugging eficiente y monitoring.

---

## SETUP (OBLIGATORIO)

```python
import logging

# Setup
logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)
logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)
```

---

## LOG LEVELS (OBLIGATORIO)

```python
# INFO - Normal operations
logger.info(f"Processing image {image_id}")
logger.info(f"Model loaded successfully")

# WARNING - Problemas no críticos
logger.warning(f"Low confidence: {conf:.2f}")

# ERROR - Errores que requieren atención
logger.error(f"Processing failed: {e}", exc_info=True)

# DEBUG - Detalles para debugging (desarrollo)
logger.debug(f"Intermediate result: {result}")
```

---

## WHAT TO LOG (RECOMENDADO)

```python
# 1. Request start
logger.info(f"Received request - File: {file.filename}")

# 2. Model inference time
start = time.time()
result = model(input)
logger.info(f"Inference time: {time.time() - start:.2f}s")

# 3. Errors
logger.error(f"Failed: {e}", exc_info=True)

# 4. Important decisions
logger.info(f"Using device: {device}")
```

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS (PROHIBIDOS)

### ❌ NEVER:
- `print()` en lugar de `logger`
- Logging de secrets/credentials
- Excessive logging (cada línea)
- No logging en error cases

---

**Logging estructurado facilita debugging en producción.**
